From 9be37df1b303469aac3027554c27798cc6e27d34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:27:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] consumer: find the dma-buf fd on MediaTek gralloc

collect_dmabufs() handed the producer anb->handle->data[0] as the
buffer's dma-buf. That holds for Qualcomm gralloc, but MediaTek's
gralloc4 puts its gralloc_extra metadata handle
(anon_inode:gralloc_extra) first and the pixel dma-buf after it. The
producer then imports a non-dma-buf fd and fails: kbase rejects it with
ENOMEM and eglCreateImageKHR returns EGL_BAD_ALLOC.

Take the first fd of the native handle that reports a size large enough
for the pixels instead. Only a dma-buf answers lseek(SEEK_END) with a
size, so on Qualcomm this still picks data[0].

Tested on a Galaxy A16 5G (SM-A166P, Dimensity 6100+, Mali-G57 MC2):
the six 1080x2160 buffers now arrive as
/dmabuf:G:SurfaceView[com.anland.consum...] and a producer renders into
them at 60 fps.

Signed-off-by: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
---
 .../app/src/main/jni/native_consumer.c          | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/consumers/anland_v5/android_consumer/app/src/main/jni/native_consumer.c b/consumers/anland_v5/android_consumer/app/src/main/jni/native_consumer.c
index 0f76298..904fba6 100644
--- a/consumers/anland_v5/android_consumer/app/src/main/jni/native_consumer.c
+++ b/consumers/anland_v5/android_consumer/app/src/main/jni/native_consumer.c
@@ -156,8 +156,23 @@ static int collect_dmabufs(struct consumer_state *s)
             continue;
         }
 
-        int fd = anb->handle->data[0];   /* first fd backs the dma-buf */
         int stride = anb->stride, width = anb->width, height = anb->height;
+        /* Qualcomm gralloc puts the pixel dma-buf first, MediaTek puts its
+         * gralloc_extra metadata handle there and the dma-buf later. Only a
+         * dma-buf reports a size, so take the first fd large enough to hold
+         * the pixels. */
+        int fd = -1;
+        for (int k = 0; k < anb->handle->numFds && fd < 0; k++) {
+            off_t size = lseek(anb->handle->data[k], 0, SEEK_END);
+            if (size >= (off_t)stride * 4 * height)
+                fd = anb->handle->data[k];
+        }
+        if (fd < 0) {
+            LOGE("no dma-buf among the %d fds of the buffer on attempt %d",
+                 anb->handle->numFds, attempt);
+            api.cancelBuffer(win, anb, -1);
+            continue;
+        }
 
         /* deduplicate by ANativeWindowBuffer pointer (stable per queue slot) */
         bool dup_found = false;
